    "text": "A snapshot is the whole state of the case at one instant. A long start-up is simulated once, and each case after it begins there, which is often most of the run time of a study saved. Set the snapshot time past the point where your case has settled. A run from the snapshot carries on from the snapshot time, so the fault is timed after it: 2.1 s here, 0.1 s after the 2 s snapshot."
